# Compiler files
cache/
out/

# Commonly ignored directories
.logs/
.ignore/

# Ignores development broadcast logs
!/broadcast
/broadcast/*/31337/
/broadcast/**/dry-run/

# Record written by the test suite
deployments/999999.json
deployments/user/999999/

# Written by scripts/check-commitment.mjs and scripts/check-tupla.mjs on every
# run. They compile a throwaway contract that calls the real library, so the
# client's hashes are compared against the compiler rather than against a second
# implementation of ours. The content changes with the case being measured, and
# committing a file a script rewrites is how generated files start disagreeing
# with what generates them — the same class as a script that deletes what it does
# not produce, seen from the other side.
test/gerado/

# Records of WHO deployed WHICH vault. `deployments/137.json` carries the
# protocol's own addresses and belongs in a public repository; this does not.
# The path itself is the data: `user/137/<owner>/vaults.json` states that a given
# address opened a given vault, and the first folder to appear here was
# 0x930BB359…, one of the Safe signers listed by `getOwners()`. On chain that
# link is discoverable; committing it here is publishing it, and those are not
# the same act.
# Only 999999 (the fork) was ignored before, because `user/137/` came into
# existence the first time someone ran against mainnet. Deleting these two lines
# restores the previous behaviour — the decision to publish is the owner's.
deployments/user/

# Docs
docs/

# Dotenv file
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Enderecos publicos em cache, para nao repetir a senha do keystore a cada execucao
.genesis-enderecos
